Presets keep the provider's order within one location

preset_discovery.cpp sorted the presets of one location (the plugin itself, a container
file) by load key, so a plugin's factory presets reached AU and VST3 hosts in alphabetical
order whatever order the plugin declared them in. Sort by location only and let the stable
sort keep the provider's order inside one: as deterministic, and the order the plugin means
(a library laid out by type).

--- a/src/detail/clap/preset_discovery.cpp
+++ b/src/detail/clap/preset_discovery.cpp
@@ -570,13 +570,16 @@
     // Factory content first: AU and VST3 numbers are positions, so a user saving a preset
     // must not renumber the plugin's own (user files would otherwise sort before presets
     // inside the plugin, by location kind).
+    // Within one location (the plugin itself, a container file) the presets keep the order
+    // the provider gave them in: as deterministic as sorting, and the order the plugin
+    // means (a library laid out by type, not by name). AU hosts show it as a flat list.
     std::stable_sort(_presets.begin(), _presets.end(),
                      [](const PresetEntry &a, const PresetEntry &b)
                      {
                        const bool userA = !a.isFactoryContent();
                        const bool userB = !b.isFactoryContent();
-                       return std::tie(userA, a.locationKind, a.location, a.loadKey) <
-                              std::tie(userB, b.locationKind, b.location, b.loadKey);
+                       return std::tie(userA, a.locationKind, a.location) <
+                              std::tie(userB, b.locationKind, b.location);
                      });
   }
 
--- a/src/detail/clap/preset_discovery.h
+++ b/src/detail/clap/preset_discovery.h
@@ -37,8 +37,10 @@
         are positional - a host stores the *index*, not the identity - so the
         same content must always produce the same numbering, or reopening a
         project silently selects a different preset. Presets are therefore
-        sorted by (location kind, location, load key), never by the order the
-        filesystem happened to hand them over.
+        sorted by (location kind, location), never by the order the
+        filesystem happened to hand them over; within one location (the plugin
+        itself, a container file) they keep the order the provider declared
+        them in, which is as deterministic and is the order the plugin means.
 */
 
 #include <atomic>
